<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/144.0.0.0 Safari/537.36" version="29.3.6">
  <diagram id="GRd6Yhnf8BJU112BtZzJ" name="Page-1">
    <mxGraphModel dx="4060" dy="2397" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1100" pageHeight="850" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="FryNYFvuJFRB2pLlbwjs-29" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Project Architecture Flow &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="260" x="-60" y="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FryNYFvuJFRB2pLlbwjs-30" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data Entity Diagram&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="320" x="-68" y="598" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FryNYFvuJFRB2pLlbwjs-96" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;fontColor=#000000;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=none;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;gradientColor=#FFF2A1;shadow=1;size=33;pointerEvents=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 102, 102);&quot;&gt;The Core Problem&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;In modern manufacturing, knowing a machine &lt;i data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;60&quot;&gt;will&lt;/i&gt; fail isn&#39;t enough. Engineers need to know &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;107&quot;&gt;why&lt;/b&gt; (e.g., Is it the heat or the vibration?) so they can fix it before the line stops. Standard AI is a &quot;black box&quot; that doesn&#39;t give reasons.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="146" width="1240" x="169" y="-548" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="FryNYFvuJFRB2pLlbwjs-97" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;Our Solution (The 3-Pillar Approach)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Intelligence (Engine):&lt;/b&gt; Member A builds a &quot;Model Zoo&quot; of 5 different AI models. Instead of just picking one, the system uses &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;128&quot;&gt;SHAP (Shapley Additive Explanations)&lt;/b&gt; to break down exactly how much credit each sensor (Temperature, Pressure, etc.) gets for a specific failure prediction.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Trust (Validation):&lt;/b&gt; Most XAI projects stop at the graph. Member B adds a &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;77&quot;&gt;Validation Layer&lt;/b&gt;. It mathematically checks if the AI&#39;s &quot;reason&quot; matches the physics of the data. If the explanation is unstable or &quot;unfaithful,&quot; the system flags it as untrustworthy.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Experience (Digital Twin):&lt;/b&gt; Instead of looking at boring spreadsheets, the user interacts with a &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;100&quot;&gt;3D Digital Twin&lt;/b&gt; of the factory. If the AI detects a high risk of failure due to Vibration, the 3D model of that specific machine physically shakes in the dashboard, making the data intuitive for non-technical factory floor managers.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;14&quot;&gt;&lt;font size=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;14&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Synergy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;By splitting the project this way, Member A ensures the math is cutting-edge and fast, while Member B ensures the insights are actionable and scientifically verified.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="296" width="1460" x="178" y="-386" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
